2026-11-06T03:02:08.7441207Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-06T03:02:08.7452586Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-06T03:02:08.7453566Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-06T03:02:08.7454296Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-06T03:02:08.7454658Z 
2026-11-06T03:02:08.7454948Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-06T03:02:08.7455367Z 
2026-11-06T03:02:08.7455718Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-06T03:02:08.7456467Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-06T03:02:08.7456865Z 
2026-11-06T03:02:08.7457072Z If you would like to
2026-11-06T03:02:08.7457549Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-06T03:02:08.7457865Z 
2026-11-06T03:02:08.7458232Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-06T03:02:08.7458846Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-11-06T03:02:08.7459026Z 
